    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: linux/dim: Fix divide by 0 in RDMA DIM (CVE-2022-49670)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: 6fire: fix use-after-free on disconnect (CVE-2026-31581)\n\n* kernel: ip6_gre: Use cached t-\u003enet in ip6erspan_changelink() (CVE-2026-46120)\n\n* kernel: sctp: purge outqueue on stale COOKIE-ECHO handling (CVE-2026-52924)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: conntrack: remove sprintf usage (CVE-2026-53002)\n\n* kernel: ice: fix double-free of tx_buf skb (CVE-2026-53009)\n\n* kernel: zram: fix use-after-free in zram_bvec_write_partial() (CVE-2026-53185)\n\n* kernel: i2c: stub: Reject I2C block transfers with invalid length (CVE-2026-64191)\n\n* kernel: net: qrtr: restrict socket creation to the initial network namespace (CVE-2026-68294)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: flowtable: publish GC-visible tuple last (CVE-2026-74746)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* RT scheduler livelock: migrate-disabled task at pushable-list head causes repeated RT push/stopper retries, starving a critical RT task (remaining issue after CVE-2026-45919 fix in 94894c9c477e) (JIRA:RHEL-257978)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
